From 6a2f5928d86e42c51bf1bf7ab490bb31582ad62a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 06:04:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): require PR landing disposition on completion
 [daveey]

Both tool and CLI completed OPEN PRs with green CI: the shared acceptance receipt only represented CI, not disposition. Local-only contracts skipped acceptance even when publishing. Existing CI fixtures asserted success for OPEN PRs and worker guidance did not name a landing handoff, so this lifecycle gap was encoded rather than detected.

Carry PR state and require closure, merge, a live exact-PR same-board landing owner rechecked in the completion write transaction, or an explicit retained left-open reason. Preserve exact-head CI and no-required-check waiver semantics; accept CLOSED as disposition, not delivery. Update schema, built-in worker guidance, docs and done notices.

RED: both actual registry tool and CLI replay completed the OPEN PR before the fix. GREEN: 307 passed, 1 skipped across 10 targeted files (48 landing cases); scripts/check --base origin/main: 15 checks passed. HTTP fixture replay names example-card / PR 621 and known abbreviated a4733f8e; its full SHA is synthetic, not invented historical evidence.
